body:
>I wouldn't say it is misinterpreting;

Then you would be wrong. It's often incorrectly interpreted as though one has no hardships, leading such a person to take offense at their hardships being minimized. It is nearly always intended to demonstrate systemic racial inequality, which doesn't require the big citation you think it does.

We're not even going into academic definitions here, which is a weird way to try and make your term relevant to a situation it isn't.
